  <p class="note-line">
    Ranges are directional, drawn from current salary-tracking sources, hiring reports, and industry coverage
    at the time of writing. Verify current figures against live postings and specific employers before making
    a financial decision.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Broad salary averages you will see quoted online — around Rs 20,000 a month for content writers and
      roughly Rs 25,000-27,000 a month for copywriters — flatten a huge amount of real variation. A generalist
      content writer competing purely on volume is now competing against AI-assisted drafting, and that
      comparison does not favour the human. A content writer with real fintech or SaaS depth, or a copywriter
      with a track record of lifting conversion rates, is playing an entirely different, better-paid game than
      the average the aggregators report.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="freelance-vs-inhouse">Freelance vs in-house: two different money games</h2>

  <p>
    This is the part most "which career is better" content skips, and it matters more than the raw salary
    numbers above.
  </p>

  <div class="feature-grid">
    {freelanceGrid.map((item) => (
